{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"TextOutputStream","kind":"identifier"}],"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"overview","text":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"You can send the output of the standard library’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"print(_:to:)"},{"type":"text","text":" and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"dump(_:to:)"},{"type":"text","text":" functions to an instance of a type that conforms to the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TextOutputStream"},{"type":"text","text":" protocol instead of to standard output. Swift’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"String"},{"type":"text","text":" type conforms to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TextOutputStream"},{"type":"text","text":" already, so you can capture"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the output from "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"print(_:to:)"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"dump(_:to:)"},{"text":" in a string instead of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"logging it to standard output.","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["var s = \"\"","for n in 1...5 {","    print(n, terminator: \"\", to: &s)","}","\/\/ s == \"12345\""]},{"level":1,"type":"heading","text":"Conforming to the TextOutputStream Protocol","anchor":"Conforming-to-the-TextOutputStream-Protocol"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"To make your custom type conform to the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TextOutputStream"},{"type":"text","text":" protocol,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"implement the required "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"write(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" method. Functions that use a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TextOutputStream"},{"type":"text","text":" target may call "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"write(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" multiple times per writing"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"operation."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"As an example, here’s an implementation of an output stream that converts"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"any input to its plain ASCII representation before sending it to standard"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"output."}]},{"code":["struct ASCIILogger: TextOutputStream {","    mutating func write(_ string: String) {","        let ascii = string.unicodeScalars.lazy.map { scalar in","            scalar == \"\\n\"","              ? \"\\n\"","              : scalar.escaped(asASCII: true)","        }","        print(ascii.joined(separator: \"\"), terminator: \"\")","    }","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ASCIILogger"},{"type":"text","text":" type’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"write(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" method processes its string input by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"escaping each Unicode scalar, with the exception of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\"\\n\""},{"type":"text","text":" line returns."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"By sending the output of the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"print(_:to:)"},{"type":"text","text":" function to an instance of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ASCIILogger"},{"type":"text","text":", you invoke its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"write(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" method."}]},{"code":["let s = \"Hearts ♡ and Diamonds ♢\"","print(s)","\/\/ Prints \"Hearts ♡ and Diamonds ♢\"","","var asciiLogger = ASCIILogger()","print(s, to: &asciiLogger)","\/\/ Prints \"Hearts \\u{2661} and Diamonds \\u{2662}\""],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"}]}],"relationshipsSections":[{"kind":"relationships","title":"Inherited By","type":"inheritedBy","identifiers":["doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/StringProtocol"]},{"kind":"relationships","identifiers":["doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/DefaultStringInterpolation","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/String","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Substring"],"type":"conformingTypes","title":"Conforming Types"}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"metadata":{"title":"TextOutputStream","externalID":"s:s16TextOutputStreamP","symbolKind":"protocol","platforms":[{"deprecated":false,"unavailable":false,"name":"iOS","beta":false,"introducedAt":"8.0"},{"deprecated":false,"unavailable":false,"beta":false,"name":"iPadOS","introducedAt":"8.0"},{"deprecated":false,"unavailable":false,"beta":false,"name":"Mac Catalyst","introducedAt":"13.0"},{"deprecated":false,"unavailable":false,"beta":false,"name":"macOS","introducedAt":"10.10"},{"beta":false,"deprecated":false,"introducedAt":"9.0","name":"tvOS","unavailable":false},{"beta":false,"deprecated":false,"introducedAt":"1.0","name":"visionOS","unavailable":false},{"deprecated":false,"unavailable":false,"beta":false,"name":"watchOS","introducedAt":"2.0"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"TextOutputStream"}],"fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"TextOutputStream","kind":"identifier"}],"roleHeading":"Protocol","modules":[{"name":"Swift"}],"role":"symbol"},"sections":[],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/TextOutputStream","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift"]]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A type that can be the target of text-streaming operations."}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/swift\/textoutputstream"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"seeAlsoSectio